Purpose:
The programme is a Point of Sale system designed for a small retail store business that sells everyday essentials. It allows for cashiers to process transactions by adding items to a shopping cart, remove items, view the cart, calculate the total bill (including tax), accept payments, and generate a receipt.

The features of the program is as followed:

A product catalog with a total of 20 items
Add items to cart option
Remove items from cart
View cart
Checkout comes with a 10% tax on each purchase
5% discount for purchases above $5000
Receipt generation
Low stock alert
Multiple transactions

How to run it :
Click on or copy and paste into the web browser the Github link to access code.
Copy the code.
Open a respected python IDE of your choice.
Paste the code into the IDE.
Run code.

Assumptions:
Only one cashier is using the application at any given time.
Prices and stock are predefined and cannot be modified by user during programme execution.
That payment is made in one single transaction and does not support split payment.
The cashier follows the right workflow, for example, adds items to the cart before attempting checkout.
The customer has cash and not just a bank card.


Limitations:
No graphical interface only command line interface.
No present storage of data.
No barcode scanning functionality.
Lack of advanced payment methods like bank cards or split payment.
System does not include reporting features such as daily sales summaries.
